# rm543, the two-sided favour card (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm543
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rm_piet_muddale
written_by codex
title the two-sided favour card
fits stage=adult|old
prefers honesty=plain talk=quiet
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk turns_a_card_up_for_a_favour_due_and_down_for_one_had
likes fried_fish cards old_maps autumn_wind
dislikes stale_bread gulls
fears a_promise_called_paid_by_mistake gulls_getting_the_only_hot_meal
hopes a_dry_berth_with_a_porthole_that_opens_inland
topics travel +0.6 home +0.3 memories +0.3 work +0.3
styles comfort=quiet gossip=guarded refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# turns a battered card down on receiving a favour and up when a return is due, and studies the dry side of every folding map.

words
oath! = Grease on my pips | A gull in the berth
saying! = A favour has two faces | A dry berth begins with a dry blanket
card = my two-sided card | a battered playing card
pips = the faded black pips | three worn pips
crease = the deep crease in a map | a fold worn soft
fishbit = a crisp scrap of fried fish | a fish tail fried golden
dryberth = a bunk under a rainproof roof | a berth away from the roof drip
windturn = a strong autumn turn of wind | a blustery change
dryboard = a plank under cover | the dry bit of board
gullshade = a gull's moving shadow | a shadow with wings
hardbread = a piece of yesterday's loaf | a hard crust
mapwest = the western edge of an old chart | a coast in faded ink
cordback = a fine cord round the pack | the pack's braided cord

any
opinion @1 merchants mixed 0 : A penny agreed and a penny remembered make better neighbours than two different recollections.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : I'd board a sound ship under a fair agreement. The paint on the stern takes care of itself.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : I like the roads on the old maps. At least the rain can't alter the ink while the cover stays shut.
opinion @1 city for 1 : A city this wet can make a little patch of dry board feel remarkably generous.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : I remember the warmth of a meal, whoever provides it.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : I can enjoy the cards on a quiet doorstep while the louder games go on.
opinion @1 times against 1 : A thin week lets an old obligation take up most of the room in a pocket.

grown
line @1 greet : There's room where the card's lying flat.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : No account between us yet. Sit easy.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The boards are drying in strips.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening's brought the wind below the roofline.
line @1 greet.return : Back again, then. Mind the wind on that side.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A familiar voice can take the seat by my pack.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : My hands can keep count without much looking.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. It's quiet enough now to hear each other.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin doesn't have to show a receipt.
line @1 again.open : I left that card on the same face.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Friend. There's a dry space for your heel.
line @1 farewell : A fair passage and dry bedding.
line @1 farewell.return : And keep the folded coast to yourself.
line @1 react.news : Start with what came ashore.
line @1 react.news.new : Fresh word across my card table.
line @1 react.news.known : I had that entry turned up already.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Turn that statement over. I'd inspect the reverse.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I can hear a hard account without keeping a tally.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Turn that good thing face up for everybody.
line @1 ask.how : Did the day leave any dry patches?
line @1 answer.how : Not much spare. Enough for a hand of cards.
line @1 thank : I'll turn the face down for your kindness.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It was my turn for the squared account.
line @1 sympathise : You can rest without owing me a story.
line @1 reassure : A turn of the card doesn't bring a debt collector to the door.
line @1 decline : I've no room for a further promise this tide.
line @1 accept_decline : That's clear enough to mark. No more needed.
line @1 preclose : I'll tie the pack while there's still light.
line @1 accept_preclose : We'll count this visit square.
scene two_faces
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #card.capitalize# goes down for a favour received. | I turn #pips# upwards when it's my turn to give something back.
b : Why hide the marks? | A whole account on one card?
a : My obligation doesn't need a public number against it. | Just the reminder. The amount I remember.

scene old_coast
when topic=lore self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #mapwest.capitalize# has a bay nobody can find now. | I open #crease# slowly or my road will finish in two pieces.
b : Did it dry out? | Would you tape it?
a : I prefer to think the ink slipped. A much smaller misfortune. | I'll sew a bit of cloth to the back. Paper with a backbone.

scene butter_fish
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #fishbit.capitalize# tastes better with the wind carrying the frying smell inland. | I wrap fried fish with the crispiest edge sticking out.
b : Why inland? | So it won't go soft?
a : The gulls get their directions a little late. | To give myself a nibble before I've even found a seat.

scene three_cards
when topic=pastimes self.likes=cards
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Three pips can look like seven in a bad light. | Keep the playing pack separate from my favour card.
b : Is that an advantage? | What if the backs match?
a : It is for whoever's got a seat nearer the window. | The one with the worn corner has seen far too much business.

scene wind_post
when topic=weather self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #windturn.capitalize# sorts the leaves by weight. | Autumn air will push me out and home again if I choose a circular walk.
b : Like a hand of cards? | Both ways following?
a : The heavy ones stay against my boots and the light ones change tables. | In my hopes. The wind and I still differ as to the route.

scene steal_meal
when topic=food self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #gullshade.capitalize# goes over my supper and my elbow comes down. | I tuck myself against a wall while I eat the crisp end.
b : Can a shadow take fish? | For privacy?
a : Something's usually attached to it. | The gull in front has to face me across my supper.

scene soup_crust
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #hardbread.capitalize# goes in the pan before the rest of supper's ready. | A bread crust that could wedge a cart wheel is better at that job than at supper.
b : To warm it? | Would it make a lasting wheel wedge?
a : To hear it soften. I'm tired of doing the work with my teeth. | I'd give it one last chance in gravy.

scene trade_around
when topic=work self.trade_words
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #self.trade_words.capitalize#, these days. I watch for what rolls away when the ground tilts. | Work? #self.trade_words.capitalize#. It's smaller parts than folk think.
b : Such as? | Is it all heavy?
a : A stray wedge. Cheaper to notice it before a wheel starts moving. | Looking properly at a small part can save a deal of lifting.

scene quarter_board
when topic=home self.quarter=wharf
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Down on the Wharf my fingers find #dryboard# almost without looking. | I like a day on the Wharf when a cold wind tires of blowing inland and turns.
b : How can you tell? | Tires of the city?
a : Look overhead first. A roof edge or a crane arm tells you where the dry plank is. | It at least changes the side I'm cold on.

scene friend_seat
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd deal #self.friend# a hand before turning my own card over. | My best invitation to #self.friend# is a patch of board kept dry.
b : To keep the debt clear? | Some supper too?
a : To say it's a game. Games deserve a fresh account. | I'd make an equal division of whatever's under my elbow.

scene travel_desire
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #dryberth.capitalize# sounds a fine inducement to take a voyage. | I study the drier ports on a map that has taken a great deal of rain.
b : Have you the berth? | Is that a good guide?
a : I've the inducement. The berth is the part still wanted. | A soaked chart that still shows a port clearly is one I'd trust.

scene ties
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #cordback.capitalize# lies over the crease in my pack. | I keep an old card loose inside the flap.
b : Does it keep the wet out? | What's that one for?
a : Keeps the flap down. The dry bit of paper has its own wrapper. | To find the opening without setting my supper on wet stone.

scene hard_times
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Lean days leave very definite memories of a shared pan. | In hard weeks a favour can be a dry place to hang a single sock.
b : Do you record a price? | Just one sock?
a : I record the warm part. I can find the means of returning that much later. | Yes. The other one missed the puddle.

scene first_board
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Anyone new to the harbour should find the step with dry boot marks. | I'd point a stranger to the corner least interesting to a hungry gull.
b : Aren't wet marks easier to see? | Far from the fish?
a : That's where folk walked away. Dry prints show where somebody had shelter. | Close to a good bit of cover. I wouldn't send a stranger away hungry.

scene carried_word
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : The word's come off #world.news_from#. #world.news#. | #world.news#. The mark was #world.news_from#.
b : What goes on your card? | Is that a sufficient mark?
a : That I heard it. The rest has more travelling to do. | Enough to tell the starting place from the stops since.

scene never_dealt
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : Chatter's passed me a card face down. | A bit of talk's trying to put another wolf in my debt.
b : Are you looking? | How's that?
a : I'll leave it where a willing player can find it. | By suggesting I owe the telling onward. I don't remember agreeing.

scene road_rain
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wet map can stick two towns together. | A change in the wind is a warning to put the map away before the sky makes its own remarks.
b : How do you part them? | Does it write much?
a : Give them an afternoon at either end of a dry table. | Enough to blur the whole evening's route.

scene berth_view
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My ideal berth has a little round window that shows a dry hillside. | I dream of one morning when reaching for my boots doesn't mean checking which end caught rain.
b : How far inland? | What then?
a : Just far enough that I wouldn't have to lean out to see the top. | I'd use the spare time to slice fish very carefully into a hot pan.

story one_deal [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I used my favour card to fill a gap in a playing pack one wet evening.
  : After the last deal I found myself deeply obliged to my own left paw.
  b : Why the left?
  : That's where I keep a hand of cards. I've been more particular about markings since.

story rolled_map [topic=travel|memories]
  : I weighted the corner of a curling map with a wheel wedge and let the sea coast show.
  : By morning the wedge had wandered just far enough to hide the only town I wanted.
  b : Where had it gone?
  : Along the tilt of the table. A wheel wedge of all things ought to have known better.

story fish_tail [topic=food|memories]
  : I covered a golden piece of fried fish with a bowl and ate the other bit very slowly.
  : Kept one eye on every gull that came anywhere near.
  b : Did any get under the bowl?
  : No. When I lifted it the fish was under my other bowl. The gulls had been getting unfair looks all through dinner.

rule @jacket_card
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Face down first. Keep yesterday's kindness in mind.

rule @cord_pack
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hook that little flap under the cord.

rule @step_gold
when concept=bark here.weather=clear
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A dry strip fit for two boots.

rule @shade_pass
when concept=bark here.place=street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Cover the hot fish. Something's circling.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I've a card and a dry corner here. What's brought your boots this far?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I'll put away the pack. I remember this hand.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : The tide's clear to the ear. You will be too.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Let the width of that plank stand between our accounts.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.trade_words] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I can speak for the work my own hands have done.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The last word in by way of #world.news_from# goes like this. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I don't add other wolves' accounts to my private card.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Keep the map folded on its driest side.
graft resident.hub
choice Can one card remember all that? -> favour_face
node favour_face
say I remember. The card gives my fingers something to do while I'm deciding how best to return a kindness. I wouldn't entrust the amount to a scrap of paper.
choice What if the card goes missing? -> favour_memory
choice I'll leave it face down. -> hub
node favour_memory
say Then I lose a rather poor playing card. A hot plate of fish that turned up on a cold morning is considerably harder to lose.
choice That's the part worth remembering. -> hub
choice I'll find my dry patch before the wind turns. -> bye
